---
import DocsLayout from "@layouts/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro:components";
---

<DocsLayout title="Installation" currentPath="/docs" toc={[
  { label: "The CLI", id: "the-cli", level: 2 },
  { label: "Existing projects", id: "existing-projects", level: 2 },
  { label: "TypeScript config", id: "typescript-config", level: 2 },
  { label: "Manual installation", id: "manual-installation", level: 2 },
]}>
  <section class="docs-hero">
    <span class="docs-label">@qwik.dev/astro</span>
    <h1>Installation</h1>
    <p class="docs-intro">
      The Qwik Astro integration automatically optimizes your project
      thanks to JavaScript Streaming.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <h2>The CLI</h2>
    <p>
      To start a new Qwik Astro project, run the command in your
      preferred package manager.
    </p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-header">
        <span class="code-filename">Terminal</span>
      </div>
      <div class="code-body">
        <Code
          code={`npm create @qwik.dev/astro@latest

# or with pnpm
pnpm create @qwik.dev/astro@latest

# or with bun
bun create @qwik.dev/astro@latest`}
          lang="bash"
          theme="github-dark"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <h2>Existing projects</h2>
    <p>
      To install <code>@qwik.dev/astro</code> in an existing project,
      run the following from your project directory and follow the
      prompts.
    </p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-header">
        <span class="code-filename">Terminal</span>
      </div>
      <div class="code-body">
        <Code
          code={`npx astro add @qwik.dev/astro

# or with pnpm
pnpm astro add @qwik.dev/astro`}
          lang="bash"
          theme="github-dark"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <h2>TypeScript config</h2>
    <p>
      The integration needs the following in <code>tsconfig.json</code>
      for TypeScript to recognize Qwik's JSX types.
    </p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-header">
        <span class="code-filename">tsconfig.json</span>
      </div>
      <div class="code-body">
        <Code
          code={`{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "jsxImportSource": "@qwik.dev/core"
  }
}`}
          lang="json"
          theme="github-dark"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      If you don't intend to use Qwik as your primary
      <code>jsxImportSource</code>, add the following at the top of
      each Qwik component file:
    </p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-header">
        <span class="code-filename">component.tsx</span>
      </div>
      <div class="code-body">
        <Code
          code={`/** @jsxImportSource @qwik.dev/core */`}
          lang="tsx"
          theme="github-dark"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-section">
    <h2>Manual installation</h2>
    <p>Install the integration and Qwik core:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-header">
        <span class="code-filename">Terminal</span>
      </div>
      <div class="code-body">
        <Code
          code={`npm install @qwik.dev/astro @qwik.dev/core`}
          lang="bash"
          theme="github-dark"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      Then add the integration to your <code>astro.config.mjs</code>:
    </p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <div class="code-header">
        <span class="code-filename">astro.config.mjs</span>
      </div>
      <div class="code-body">
        <Code
          code={`import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';
import qwik from '@qwik.dev/astro';

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [qwik()],
});`}
          lang="js"
          theme="github-dark"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .docs-hero {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--neutral-950);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .docs-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--rose-500);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
  }

  .docs-intro {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--neutral-400);
    max-width: 48ch;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .docs-section {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--neutral-950);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .docs-section:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
  }

  p {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    color: var(--neutral-400);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  p code {
    color: var(--green-400);
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .code-block {
    border: 1px solid var(--neutral-950);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .code-header {
    background-color: #1a1a1a;
    padding: var(--space-3xs) var(--space-m);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--neutral-950);
  }

  .code-filename {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--neutral-400);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .code-body {
    padding: var(--space-m);
    background-color: #151515;
  }

  .code-body :global(pre) {
    background: transparent !important;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
